      "test": "test_d28_gate_1_stays_green_at_every_commit_never_only_at_the_last",
      "obligation": "D28",
      "grounds": "INSENSITIVE BY CONSTRUCTION. D28's subject is the commit set `git rev-list 6fb4d92..HEAD -- .agent/decisions/m3u6a1-surgery.py tests examples` returns, and every mutation this catalogue can express edits the WORKING TREE alone, leaving that history byte-identical. No reversion or sensitivity row can turn it red, so a row for it would certify only that the clause ignores the mutation. It was also RED at the `6fb4d92` baseline, so it already holds the red credential this instrument exists to supply for clauses that are green there. Its ~340 s cost and its one nested worktree per revision are consequences of the exclusion, never its grounds."
    }
